    "method": "hand-built and checked by lab replay: walk right (stick full right, every input) off the floor into the sideways spring (rotation -90, the Course 5 Spring (2)'s SpringScript: upForce 50, strength 220). The hit on tick 20 sets Velocity (0, 450) and momentum (3520, 125) with the spring cutscene (inputs held until it ends, tick 33). The launch meets the overhang's down-left face on tick 25 and slides along it 26.6, 26.2, 25.7 ... 25.5 u a tick down (ticks 26-42; y 94.1 on tick 24 to -350.5 on tick 42: 444.6 u in 18 ticks, momentum.x decaying exactly as in the air), leaves its bottom corner on tick 43 falling at the ordinary rate (0.8 u, as the ghost's fall at the same Velocity.y) and is in the finish band (y -600 to -400) on tick 50. 90 inputs so a playback shows the ghost to its end. Ghost path: its first 90 physics ticks (--path-ticks 90), as every ghost on this lab."
